<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - SA Bias H1 EPS up, plans delisting.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SA Bias H1 EPS up, plans delisting.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		17.1	  vs 4.8</p>
<p>    - attrib		  16.5	  vs 4.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 5.0	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   4.71	  vs 1.36</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   7.42	  vs 1.68</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.30	  vs 0.13</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.64	  vs 2.17</p>
<p>    Turnover		  124.32	vs 118.22</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.31 loss   vs nil</p>
<p>Div payable September 5</p>
<p>on register August 22</p>
<p>Full name: SA Bias Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that proposals to delist the group from the Johannesburg Stock Exchange were published last month. The firm would be constituted as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Sabhold Group Ltd, which in turn is a wholly-owned unit of Sabvest Ltd and owns 90.1 percent of SA Bias. A cash distribution of 270 cents a share will be made to shareholders.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
